  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/D0529F">Example <span data-tag="D0529F">6.3.5.20</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-topos, and let $e_{\calX }: \LGeom \rightarrow \widehat{\SSet }$ be the functor represented by $\calX $. Proposition <a href="/tag/37047A" data-tag="37047A">6.3.5.14</a> implies that $e_{\calX }$ belongs to $\widehat{\Shv }( \LGeom ^{op} )$. We will say that a sheaf $F \in \widehat{\Shv }( \LGeom ^{op} )$ is <em>representable</em> if $F \simeq e_{\calX }$ for some $\infty $-topos $\calX $. </p>
